GET {{tlsPrivateCaUrl}}/tls

::: post
test("served with a certificate from a private CA", () => {
  expect(res.json().profile).toBe("private-ca");
});

::: docs
The CA is certs/ca.pem. It is not in the system store, so this is an unknown issuer warning.
On Linux, start Postino with SSL_CERT_FILE set to the absolute path of certs/ca.pem and the
response comes without a warning, as long as "Use system certificates" is on.
